1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,500
THE CROWD — The Chat Is the Monster.
Silent demo of the simulated browser mode.

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:16,500
On-screen Italian: "TI HA VISTO" = "IT HAS SEEN YOU."
The creature watches the streamer avatar.

3
00:00:16,500 --> 00:00:28,000
"IL TESTIMONE" = "THE WITNESS."
The chat's choices have determined the ending.

4
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:37,000
Viewer messages influence the creature's trust and fear.
Participants become cells in its collective body.

5
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:46,000
The witness is one of three endings:
guardian, predator, or witness.

6
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:56,000
"C'È QUALCOSA DIETRO QUELLE FINESTRE" =
"THERE IS SOMETHING BEHIND THOSE WINDOWS."

7
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:06,000
This browser demo uses simulated viewers.
It does not prove a live Twitch connection.

8
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:18,000
Chat and raid simulation change the creature's behavior.
Simulated events are not real Twitch EventSub events.

9
00:01:18,000 --> 00:01:28,000
The game can be displayed as a broadcaster scene.
A real Twitch feed requires authorized EventSub setup.

10
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:40,100
BUILT WITH OPENAI CODEX.
The ending logic is in crowd-ending.mjs.
Codex session ID is documented in the repository.
